guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:advanced_rack=Advanced Kitchen Rack
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:advanced_rack.1=The Advanced Kitchen Rack has 9 slots in two fixed rows: 5 upper slots for oil pots/seasoning bottles, and 4 lower hooks for kitchen knives, the kitchen shovel, Flint and Steel, and similar tools.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:advanced_rack.2=The first inserted item establishes a slot filter. Oil-pot states share one family, and empty/pending/special seasoning bottles share one family.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:advanced_rack.3=Aim at a specific slot and use: hold an accepted item to insert it, or use an empty hand to withdraw it. Sneak-use an occupied slot to swap with the held item.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:advanced_rack.4=Use range is 8 blocks. Breaking the rack stores its contents and filters on the dropped item, which are restored when placed again.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:advanced_rack.5=Crafting-table pattern (· = empty):\nIII\n·R·\nSSS\nI = Iron Ingot；R = Kitchenware Racks；S = Any wooden slab
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:advanced_rack.6=Sneak-use an empty slot with an empty hand to clear its filter. /kaleidoscope_grilling:rack returns matching inventory stacks to the nearest rack within 8 blocks, following existing filters without opening a form.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:beef_chunks=Beef Chunks
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:beef_chunks.1=With Cookery 1.6.1 and the family Chopping Board extension, place one raw Beef on the board, cut four times with a Kitchen Knife, then use the knife once more to release two Beef Chunks. The chunks replace this input's normal Cow Offal output.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:braised_chicken_wings=Braised Chicken Wings
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:braised_chicken_wings.1=Use the updated Cookery Wok. Let a pot that was already active or holding a result in an older version finish through its original flow, then empty it before starting a new batch.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:braised_chicken_wings.2=The first card is an exact-count recipe and takes priority, producing the base dish without a quality bonus. The second card shows one of each required flex ingredient. Increase any of those counts up to 9 items in total; the output remains 1 dish. Quality improves as the proportions approach the target determined by the world and this recipe.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:braised_chicken_wings.3=Adding oil to an empty heated wok starts 60 seconds of preparation. Adding or removing ingredients does not restart that time; removing the heat pauses it. Ingredients must be ordinary stackable items. Custom-named items and items carrying extra data remain in your hand.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:braised_chicken_wings.4=With ingredients in the wok, the first Kitchen Shovel stir starts 10 seconds of cooking and counts as stir 1. Stir 3 times in total before completion. Cooking also starts when preparation time runs out. Ordinary ingredients cannot be added or removed after cooking starts; seasoning still follows its normal rules.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:braised_chicken_wings.5=Fewer than 3 stirs at completion produces Suspicious Stir-Fry. Leave a finished dish heated for 40 seconds and it becomes Dark Cuisine. Another 20 seconds turns it into 1–3 Charcoal and clears the wok. Removing the heat pauses these countdowns.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:braised_chicken_wings.6=Use 1 bowl to serve 1 dish, retaining hot-food and seasoning effects. Flex quality changes the food values and survives cooling. The nutrition shown on this page is the base value for the exact recipe. Dark Cuisine does not inherit the original dish's quality, heat, or seasoning.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:braised_chicken_wings.7=During preparation, use an empty hand or an ingredient container to take back the last ingredient. Taking ingredients from a hot wok, or touching a finished hot wok without a bowl or Kitchen Shovel, deals 1 damage. Stir with a shovel and serve with a bowl.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_oil_bucket=Canola Oil Bucket
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_oil_bucket.1=All three Grilling oil buckets can be placed into the world as fluids. A source flows downward first, then horizontally, using 8 visual levels.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_oil_bucket.2=An empty bucket can collect an oil source, and a Cookery Oil Pot can also take matching oil directly from a source.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_oil_bucket.3=On Bedrock these oils are script-simulated, so they do not promise every vanilla water/lava interaction. When an oil bucket is used on a Big Vat or Cookery Oil Pot, the container interaction takes priority.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_oil_bucket.4=Canola Oil gives about 60 seconds of Hot Food time, Secret Chili Oil about 10 minutes, and Premium Chili Oil about 20 minutes. Remaining heat is shown on the food lore.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_oil_bucket.5=Use: transfer oil with buckets, vats and the Cookery Oil Pot. Brush the grill with the filled Oil Pot, not a legacy oil brush.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_oil_bucket.6=Acquisition: collect it with a bucket from the vat receiving a completed oil-press batch.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_powder=Canola Powder
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_powder.1=Required setup: install the complete family bundle for this release, containing Cookery 1.6.1 with the millstone compatibility repair already applied. Updating Grilling alone, or enabling the compatibility pack alongside untouched Cookery, does not fix input loading.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_powder.2=Get canola seeds by breaking short grass while wearing a Cookery straw hat; grow on farmland. Craft 8 powders around 1 wheat into an Oil Cake; 4 cakes make one oil-press batch.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_powder.3=Grinding: hold Canola Seeds in your main hand and use it on a Cookery Millstone. Load up to 8 of the same input; each produces 1 Canola Powder. Use the raw input directly: no drying or roasting step, and no vanilla Grindstone.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_powder.4=Bring an adult cow or sheep onto the intact 3×3 millstone. Horses/donkeys must be tamed and unridden. A worker drives the loaded batch for about 100 ticks (5 seconds); collect powder ejected at the front. Sneak-use with an empty hand releases the worker. See Workstations → Millstone & Grinding for crafting and troubleshooting.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_seeds=Canola Seeds
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_seeds.1=Acquisition and farming: break short grass in Survival while wearing a Cookery Straw Hat for a chance to obtain it. Plant on farmland and harvest when mature.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_seeds.2=Mill Canola Seeds in the Cookery Millstone to obtain Canola Powder.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:canola_seeds.3=At a crafting table, surround 1 Wheat with 8 Canola Powder to make 1 Oil Cake; 4 cakes make one press batch.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:carrot_dice=Carrot Dice
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:carrot_dice.1=Use 1 Carrot on an empty Cookery Chopping Board. Use a Kitchen Knife for 4 cuts, then use it once more to release 3 Carrot Dice; collect the output.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:chicken_skin=Chicken Skin
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:chicken_skin.1=With Cookery 1.6.1 and the family Chopping Board extension, place one raw Chicken on the board, cut four times with a Kitchen Knife, then use the knife once more to release the original three Raw Meat Cuts and one Bone, plus 1–3 Chicken Skin. Killing chickens does not yield skin.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:chicken_wing=Chicken Wing
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:chicken_wing.1=Killing a chicken with a Cookery kitchen knife drops Chicken Wings; Looting can increase the amount.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:chicken_wing.2=Chicken Skin and Chicken Wings both feed into fixed skewer recipes.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:cold_houttuynia=Dressed Houttuynia
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:cold_houttuynia.1=Obtain Houttuynia from Nether fortress chest loot: a 65% chance adds 1–6 plants in total. Not every chest contains it; already-generated contents are not refilled. Keep a plant to grow on farmland or soul sand. The chest reward matches Java; Java’s replacement of about 25% of wart in newly generated fortresses is not implemented.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:cold_houttuynia.2=Hold at least 3 Houttuynia in your main hand and a Cookery Oil Pot containing Premium Chili Oil in your offhand. Sneak-use the crafting table to make 1 Dressed Houttuynia; standing nearby alone does nothing.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:cold_houttuynia.3=Crafting consumes 3 Houttuynia and 2 Premium Chili Oil points; any remaining oil stays in the pot.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:cold_houttuynia.4=Cold Houttuynia grants about 60 seconds of Fire Resistance when eaten.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:dark_grilling=Dark Grilling
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:dark_grilling.1=Break it after overcooking: the batch becomes Dark Grilling.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:dark_grilling.2=Eating side effect: Blindness for about 10 seconds.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:dragon_egg_powder=Dragon Egg Powder
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:dragon_egg_powder.1=Add Dragon Egg Powder to seasoning and eat it hot to gain Dragon Blood: increased maximum health plus a separate 2-point damage-absorption pool.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:dragon_egg_powder.2=1–3 Dragon Egg Powder uses the lower health-boost level; 4 or more uses the higher level.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:dragon_egg_powder.3=Houttuynia Powder extends Dragon Blood using the same ×2 / ×4 rule; Dragon Blood does not trigger after the food goes cold.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:dragon_egg_powder.4=Acquire: use a kitchen knife on a dragon egg for 1 to 1+Looting powder and one durability attempt (Unbreaking applies). The egg is not consumed and retains its vanilla teleport behavior.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:dragon_egg_powder.5=Bedrock currently adds 4/8 maximum health plus a separate 2-point damage buffer. This is an approximation, not Java's direct 6/10 maximum-health increase.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_chili_powder=Green Chili Powder
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_chili_powder.1=Required setup: install the complete family bundle for this release, containing Cookery 1.6.1 with the millstone compatibility repair already applied. Updating Grilling alone, or enabling the compatibility pack alongside untouched Cookery, does not fix input loading.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_chili_powder.2=Obtain chili seeds by breaking short grass while wearing a Cookery straw hat. Plant on farmland and harvest mature chili: it yields red chili, with a 20% bonus chance of green chili. Use the matching color; the two powder inputs are not interchangeable.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_chili_powder.3=Grinding: hold Green Chili in your main hand and use it on a Cookery Millstone. Load up to 8 of the same input; each produces 1 Green Chili Powder. Use the raw input directly: no drying or roasting step, and no vanilla Grindstone.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_chili_powder.4=Bring an adult cow or sheep onto the intact 3×3 millstone. Horses/donkeys must be tamed and unridden. A worker drives the loaded batch for about 100 ticks (5 seconds); collect powder ejected at the front. Sneak-use with an empty hand releases the worker. See Workstations → Millstone & Grinding for crafting and troubleshooting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_chili_powder.5=Use: one of the three required seasoning bases. Each bottle needs at least one Green Chili Powder, Sichuan Pepper and Onion Powder.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_pepper_squid_tentacles=Green Pepper Squid Tentacles
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_pepper_squid_tentacles.1=Use the updated Cookery Wok. Let a pot that was already active or holding a result in an older version finish through its original flow, then empty it before starting a new batch.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_pepper_squid_tentacles.2=The first card is an exact-count recipe and takes priority, producing the base dish without a quality bonus. The second card shows one of each required flex ingredient. Increase any of those counts up to 9 items in total; the output remains 1 dish. Quality improves as the proportions approach the target determined by the world and this recipe.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_pepper_squid_tentacles.3=Adding oil to an empty heated wok starts 60 seconds of preparation. Adding or removing ingredients does not restart that time; removing the heat pauses it. Ingredients must be ordinary stackable items. Custom-named items and items carrying extra data remain in your hand.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_pepper_squid_tentacles.4=With ingredients in the wok, the first Kitchen Shovel stir starts 10 seconds of cooking and counts as stir 1. Stir 3 times in total before completion. Cooking also starts when preparation time runs out. Ordinary ingredients cannot be added or removed after cooking starts; seasoning still follows its normal rules.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_pepper_squid_tentacles.5=Fewer than 3 stirs at completion produces Suspicious Stir-Fry. Leave a finished dish heated for 40 seconds and it becomes Dark Cuisine. Another 20 seconds turns it into 1–3 Charcoal and clears the wok. Removing the heat pauses these countdowns.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_pepper_squid_tentacles.6=Use 1 bowl to serve 1 dish, retaining hot-food and seasoning effects. Flex quality changes the food values and survives cooling. The nutrition shown on this page is the base value for the exact recipe. Dark Cuisine does not inherit the original dish's quality, heat, or seasoning.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:green_pepper_squid_tentacles.7=During preparation, use an empty hand or an ingredient container to take back the last ingredient. Taking ingredients from a hot wok, or touching a finished hot wok without a bowl or Kitchen Shovel, deals 1 damage. Stir with a shovel and serve with a bowl.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia=Houttuynia
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia.1=Obtain Houttuynia from Nether fortress chest loot: a 65% chance adds 1–6 plants in total. Not every chest contains it; already-generated contents are not refilled. Keep a plant to grow on farmland or soul sand. The chest reward matches Java; Java’s replacement of about 25% of wart in newly generated fortresses is not implemented.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia.2=Grow Houttuynia on farmland or soul sand. Chop it into Minced Houttuynia, grind it into powder, or use it for Dressed Houttuynia and stir-fried pork.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia.3=Houttuynia can also go into a Composter. Each item has a 65% chance to raise the compost level by one.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_powder=Houttuynia Powder
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_powder.1=Required setup: install the complete family bundle for this release, containing Cookery 1.6.1 with the millstone compatibility repair already applied. Updating Grilling alone, or enabling the compatibility pack alongside untouched Cookery, does not fix input loading.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_powder.2=Obtain Houttuynia from Nether fortress chest loot: a 65% chance adds 1–6 plants in total. Not every chest contains it; already-generated contents are not refilled. Keep a plant to grow on farmland or soul sand. The chest reward matches Java; Java’s replacement of about 25% of wart in newly generated fortresses is not implemented.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_powder.3=Grinding: hold Houttuynia in your main hand and use it on a Cookery Millstone. Load up to 8 of the same input; each produces 1 Houttuynia Powder. Use the raw input directly: no drying or roasting step, and no vanilla Grindstone.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_powder.4=Bring an adult cow or sheep onto the intact 3×3 millstone. Horses/donkeys must be tamed and unridden. A worker drives the loaded batch for about 100 ticks (5 seconds); collect powder ejected at the front. Sneak-use with an empty hand releases the worker. See Workstations → Millstone & Grinding for crafting and troubleshooting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_powder.5=Without Houttuynia Powder, regular seasoning effects have a base duration of about 3 minutes.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_powder.6=Adding 1–3 Houttuynia Powder multiplies seasoning-effect duration by 2; 4 or more multiplies it by 4.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_powder.7=Numb uses the same duration multiplier.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_stir_fried_pork=Houttuynia Stir-fried Pork
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_stir_fried_pork.1=Obtain Houttuynia from Nether fortress chest loot: a 65% chance adds 1–6 plants in total. Not every chest contains it; already-generated contents are not refilled. Keep a plant to grow on farmland or soul sand. The chest reward matches Java; Java’s replacement of about 25% of wart in newly generated fortresses is not implemented.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_stir_fried_pork.2=Use the updated Cookery Wok. Let a pot that was already active or holding a result in an older version finish through its original flow, then empty it before starting a new batch.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_stir_fried_pork.3=The first card is an exact-count recipe and takes priority, producing the base dish without a quality bonus. The second card shows one of each required flex ingredient. Increase any of those counts up to 9 items in total; the output remains 1 dish. Quality improves as the proportions approach the target determined by the world and this recipe.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_stir_fried_pork.4=Adding oil to an empty heated wok starts 60 seconds of preparation. Adding or removing ingredients does not restart that time; removing the heat pauses it. Ingredients must be ordinary stackable items. Custom-named items and items carrying extra data remain in your hand.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_stir_fried_pork.5=With ingredients in the wok, the first Kitchen Shovel stir starts 10 seconds of cooking and counts as stir 1. Stir 3 times in total before completion. Cooking also starts when preparation time runs out. Ordinary ingredients cannot be added or removed after cooking starts; seasoning still follows its normal rules.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_stir_fried_pork.6=Fewer than 3 stirs at completion produces Suspicious Stir-Fry. Leave a finished dish heated for 40 seconds and it becomes Dark Cuisine. Another 20 seconds turns it into 1–3 Charcoal and clears the wok. Removing the heat pauses these countdowns.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_stir_fried_pork.7=Use 1 bowl to serve 1 dish, retaining hot-food and seasoning effects. Flex quality changes the food values and survives cooling. The nutrition shown on this page is the base value for the exact recipe. Dark Cuisine does not inherit the original dish's quality, heat, or seasoning.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:houttuynia_stir_fried_pork.8=During preparation, use an empty hand or an ingredient container to take back the last ingredient. Taking ingredients from a hot wok, or touching a finished hot wok without a bowl or Kitchen Shovel, deals 1 damage. Stir with a shovel and serve with a bowl.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:minced_houttuynia=Minced Houttuynia
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:minced_houttuynia.1=Obtain Houttuynia from Nether fortress chest loot: a 65% chance adds 1–6 plants in total. Not every chest contains it; already-generated contents are not refilled. Keep a plant to grow on farmland or soul sand. The chest reward matches Java; Java’s replacement of about 25% of wart in newly generated fortresses is not implemented.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:minced_houttuynia.2=Use 1 Houttuynia on an empty Cookery Chopping Board. Use a Kitchen Knife for 4 cuts, then use it once more to release 1 Minced Houttuynia; collect the output.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:mysterious_skewer=Mysterious Skewer
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:mysterious_skewer.1=Break it during other incomplete post-oil stages: the contents become Mysterious Skewers.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:mysterious_skewer.2=Eating side effect: Nausea for about 5 seconds.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_cake=Oil Cake
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_cake.1=Crafting-table pattern (· = empty):\nPPP\nPWP\nPPP\nP = Canola Powder；W = Wheat
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_cake.2=Use: four Oil Cakes fill an Oil Press. A completed batch yields four buckets of Canola Oil and four Oil Residues.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_residue=Oil Residue
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_residue.1=Oil Residue is an oil-press by-product, with 4 produced per batch. Using it on a supported plant makes 2 consecutive bone-meal attempts, each following that plant's own growth rules.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_residue.2=Supports Canola, Onion, Sweet Potato, Houttuynia, Sichuan Pepper Saplings, Wheat, Carrots, and Potatoes.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_residue.3=Also supports Cocoa, Sweet Berry Bushes, Pink Petals, berry-free Cave Vines, Sunflowers, Lilacs, Rose Bushes, Peonies, Short Grass, Ferns, Pumpkin Stems, Melon Stems, Rooted Dirt, Twisting Vines, Weeping Vines, Mangrove Leaves, and dry hanging Mangrove Propagules. Other plants still need individual adapters.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_residue.4=Each valid use consumes only 1 Oil Residue in total; unavailable growth actions and unsupported targets consume none. Creative mode consumes none. Each pepper attempt has a 45% growth chance. Two failed rolls or blocked headroom above short grass still count as a valid use.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_residue.5=A non-sneaking main-hand use on a fruiting Sweet Berry Bush harvests it without using Oil Residue. Sneaking or an actual offhand use can still fertilize a partly grown bush; a fully grown bush consumes none.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_residue.6=Cocoa advances one stage per attempt. Cave Vines gain Glow Berries without extending. Short Grass and Ferns become tall plants when there is room above. Mangrove Leaves grow a hanging propagule into dry air below. Dry hanging propagules mature one stage per attempt, up to stage 4. Grounded or waterlogged propagules are not supported.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_residue.7=Each attempt on an intact tall flower drops one matching item. Pink Petals gain one flower until full, then drop one item per attempt. One Oil Residue can produce 2 items from full petals or tall flowers. Disabling block drops prevents those items but still consumes one Oil Residue.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_residue.8=Immature stems gain 2–5 stages per attempt. On reaching maturity, they attempt fruit growth using light, farmland, and neighboring stems; a blocked random direction produces no fruit. Mature stems cannot be fertilized again. Rooted Dirt grows Hanging Roots into air below it. Twisting Vines grow upward and Weeping Vines downward from their connected tip into air; age 25 still accepts fertilizer.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:onion=Onion
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:onion.1=Acquisition and farming: break short grass in Survival while wearing a Cookery Straw Hat for a chance to obtain it. Plant on farmland and harvest when mature.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:onion_powder=Onion Powder
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:onion_powder.1=Required setup: install the complete family bundle for this release, containing Cookery 1.6.1 with the millstone compatibility repair already applied. Updating Grilling alone, or enabling the compatibility pack alongside untouched Cookery, does not fix input loading.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:onion_powder.2=Obtain onions by breaking short grass while wearing a Cookery straw hat. Plant onions on farmland, harvest mature crops and retain some for replanting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:onion_powder.3=Grinding: hold Onion in your main hand and use it on a Cookery Millstone. Load up to 8 of the same input; each produces 1 Onion Powder. Use the raw input directly: no drying or roasting step, and no vanilla Grindstone.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:onion_powder.4=Bring an adult cow or sheep onto the intact 3×3 millstone. Horses/donkeys must be tamed and unridden. A worker drives the loaded batch for about 100 ticks (5 seconds); collect powder ejected at the front. Sneak-use with an empty hand releases the worker. See Workstations → Millstone & Grinding for crafting and troubleshooting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:onion_powder.5=Use: one of the three required seasoning bases. Each bottle needs at least one Green Chili Powder, Sichuan Pepper and Onion Powder.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:ordinary_skewer="Ordinary" Skewer
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:ordinary_skewer.1=The “Ordinary” Skewer recipe is Poisonous Potato → Spider Eye → Pufferfish. It has no normal raw-to-cooked conversion.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:ordinary_skewer.2=Eating it directly triggers a lethal challenge; without Invincible, you die.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:ordinary_skewer.3=If you first gain Invincible from a Golden Skewer, the challenge consumes Invincible and randomly resolves as Strongest Shield or Strongest Spear. Only the Shield outcome blocks the lethal result.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:ordinary_skewer.4=Ingredient order: Poisonous Potato → Spider Eye → Pufferfish
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:ordinary_skewer.5=Craft an empty Unfinished Skewer from one stick and equip it offhand. Hold a skewerable ingredient in the main hand and use it on a block to add one ingredient.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:ordinary_skewer.6=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_honey=Pepper Honey
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_honey.1=Eating effects: Numb 60 seconds
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:potato_beef_stew=Potato Beef Stew (Grilling Edition)
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:potato_beef_stew.1=Use water as the stockpot base; cook for 15 seconds and serve with a bowl. Exact recipes are listed; flexible recipes are not presented as reduced quantities.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:potato_slice=Potato Slice
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:potato_slice.1=Use 1 Potato on an empty Cookery Chopping Board. Use a Kitchen Knife for 4 cuts, then use it once more to release 3 Potato Slice; collect the output.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:premium_chili_oil_bucket=Lava Chili Oil Bucket
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:premium_chili_oil_bucket.1=Obtain Houttuynia from Nether fortress chest loot: a 65% chance adds 1–6 plants in total. Not every chest contains it; already-generated contents are not refilled. Keep a plant to grow on farmland or soul sand. The chest reward matches Java; Java’s replacement of about 25% of wart in newly generated fortresses is not implemented.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:premium_chili_oil_bucket.2=All three Grilling oil buckets can be placed into the world as fluids. A source flows downward first, then horizontally, using 8 visual levels.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:premium_chili_oil_bucket.3=An empty bucket can collect an oil source, and a Cookery Oil Pot can also take matching oil directly from a source.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:premium_chili_oil_bucket.4=On Bedrock these oils are script-simulated, so they do not promise every vanilla water/lava interaction. When an oil bucket is used on a Big Vat or Cookery Oil Pot, the container interaction takes priority.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:premium_chili_oil_bucket.5=Canola Oil gives about 60 seconds of Hot Food time, Secret Chili Oil about 10 minutes, and Premium Chili Oil about 20 minutes. Remaining heat is shown on the food lore.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:premium_chili_oil_bucket.6=Use: transfer oil with buckets, vats and the Cookery Oil Pot. Brush the grill with the filled Oil Pot, not a legacy oil brush.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:raw_mantou_slice=Raw Mantou Slice
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:raw_mantou_slice.1=Use 1 Mantou on an empty Cookery Chopping Board. Use a Kitchen Knife for 4 cuts, then use it once more to release 3 Raw Mantou Slice; collect the output.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:raw_sweet_potato_sheet=Raw Sweet Potato Sheet
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:raw_sweet_potato_sheet.1=Full route: grind Sweet Potato into Sweet Potato Powder, then use the board below. Alternatively, hold-use the powder for 1.5 seconds to knead the entire held stack into the same number of Raw Sweet Potato Sheets.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:raw_sweet_potato_sheet.2=Use 1 Sweet Potato Powder on an empty Cookery Chopping Board. Use a Kitchen Knife for 4 cuts, then use it once more to release 1 Raw Sweet Potato Sheet; collect the output.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:red_chili_powder=Red Chili Powder
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:red_chili_powder.1=Required setup: install the complete family bundle for this release, containing Cookery 1.6.1 with the millstone compatibility repair already applied. Updating Grilling alone, or enabling the compatibility pack alongside untouched Cookery, does not fix input loading.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:red_chili_powder.2=Obtain chili seeds by breaking short grass while wearing a Cookery straw hat. Plant on farmland and harvest mature chili: it yields red chili, with a 20% bonus chance of green chili. Use the matching color; the two powder inputs are not interchangeable.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:red_chili_powder.3=Grinding: hold Red Chili in your main hand and use it on a Cookery Millstone. Load up to 8 of the same input; each produces 1 Red Chili Powder. Use the raw input directly: no drying or roasting step, and no vanilla Grindstone.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:red_chili_powder.4=Bring an adult cow or sheep onto the intact 3×3 millstone. Horses/donkeys must be tamed and unridden. A worker drives the loaded batch for about 100 ticks (5 seconds); collect powder ejected at the front. Sneak-use with an empty hand releases the worker. See Workstations → Millstone & Grinding for crafting and troubleshooting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:red_chili_powder.5=Used in: Chili Oil Bucket
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:red_sweet_potato_porridge=Sweet Potato Rice Porridge
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:red_sweet_potato_porridge.1=Use water as the stockpot base; cook for 15 seconds and serve with a bowl. Exact recipes are listed; flexible recipes are not presented as reduced quantities.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:red_sweet_potato_porridge.2=Eating effects: Flatulence 45 seconds；Warmth 45 seconds
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:roasted_chicken_wing=Roasted Chicken Wing
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:roasted_chicken_wing.1=Obtain Chicken Wings by killing a chicken with a Cookery Kitchen Knife in your main hand. Looting can increase the drops.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:roasted_chicken_wing.2=Cook 1 Chicken Wing into 1 Roasted Chicken Wing. Put it in a Furnace or Smoker with fuel, then collect it from the output slot. Alternatively, place it on a lit Campfire or Soul Campfire and pick up the cooked item when it drops.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:roasted_sweet_potato=Roasted Sweet Potato
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:roasted_sweet_potato.1=Eating effects: Warmth 30 seconds
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_chili_oil_bucket=Chili Oil Bucket
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_chili_oil_bucket.1=All three Grilling oil buckets can be placed into the world as fluids. A source flows downward first, then horizontally, using 8 visual levels.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_chili_oil_bucket.2=An empty bucket can collect an oil source, and a Cookery Oil Pot can also take matching oil directly from a source.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_chili_oil_bucket.3=On Bedrock these oils are script-simulated, so they do not promise every vanilla water/lava interaction. When an oil bucket is used on a Big Vat or Cookery Oil Pot, the container interaction takes priority.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_chili_oil_bucket.4=Canola Oil gives about 60 seconds of Hot Food time, Secret Chili Oil about 10 minutes, and Premium Chili Oil about 20 minutes. Remaining heat is shown on the food lore.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_chili_oil_bucket.5=Use: transfer oil with buckets, vats and the Cookery Oil Pot. Brush the grill with the filled Oil Pot, not a legacy oil brush.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_skewer=Secret Mix Skewer
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_skewer.1=Three skewerable ingredients that do not match a fixed recipe become a Secret Skewer, storing the actual ingredients and creator information.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_skewer.2=Secret Skewer nutrition is calculated from the actual edible ingredients rather than a fixed table; duplicate ingredients reduce the final nutrition yield.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:secret_skewer.3=An uncooked Secret Skewer can be sneak-disassembled. Once cooked, it retains the ingredient information used for nutrition.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:sichuan_pepper=Sichuan Pepper
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sichuan_pepper.1=Find your first pepper tree in newly generated biomes tagged as forest. Generation is random and does not retrofit explored terrain. Harvest fruiting leaves for pepper; breaking leaves can drop saplings for replanting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sichuan_pepper.2=Sichuan Pepper is one of the three base ingredients required to finish Special Seasoning.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sichuan_pepper.3=At 4 or more Sichuan Pepper in the same bottle, eating the food hot also triggers Numb for a base duration of about 45 seconds.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sichuan_pepper.4=Houttuynia Powder extends those 45 seconds using the same ×2 or ×4 rule.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sichuan_pepper.5=Acquisition: empty-hand harvest a fruiting pepper leaf for 1–2 Sichuan Peppers.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_plate=Skewer Plate
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_plate.1=Acquisition: sneak-use a main-hand skewer on the top of a table or solid block to place a skewer plate. Recovering the plate preserves its contents.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_plate.2=A Skewer Plate stores up to 5 skewers. Use a skewer on it to add one; use an empty hand to remove the most recently inserted skewer.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_plate.3=Eating from a plate with several skewers consumes the one with the highest base nutrition first.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_plate.4=A non-empty plate can be sneak-placed, and its stored skewer data is preserved when carried again.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_plate.5=The server can disable plate priority on Cookery tables. Sneak-using a held skewer then keeps Cookery’s original table display interaction.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_plate.6=Held plates arrange their 1–5 saved servings of fixed, ordinary, and custom skewers. Each hand reads its own plate. An external skewer without a matching model leaves its position empty while preserving the stored food.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_recipe_book=Skewer Recipe Book
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_recipe_book.1=Craft four paper in a 2×2 square into an empty Skewer Recipe Book. This Bedrock acquisition bridge replaces the blank recipe item absent from public Cookery.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_recipe_book.2=Use the blank book in your main hand with a complete raw skewer in your offhand to record it. The original skewer is retained.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_recipe_book.3=Use the recorded book with an empty Unfinished Skewer in your offhand to craft from inventory. Craft that empty starter from one stick first.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_recipe_book.4=Place a recorded book on a horizontal block face, then use a stick or empty starter on it to craft. Missing ingredients or inventory space cancel crafting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:skewer_recipe_book.5=Craft a book by itself to clear its record. As in Java, secret recipes copy the recorded ingredient metadata rather than the newly consumed ingredients.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:sour_spicy_noodles=Sour and Spicy Noodles
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sour_spicy_noodles.1=Obtain Houttuynia from Nether fortress chest loot: a 65% chance adds 1–6 plants in total. Not every chest contains it; already-generated contents are not refilled. Keep a plant to grow on farmland or soul sand. The chest reward matches Java; Java’s replacement of about 25% of wart in newly generated fortresses is not implemented.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sour_spicy_noodles.2=Use water as the stockpot base; cook for 15 seconds and serve with a bowl. Exact recipes are listed; flexible recipes are not presented as reduced quantities.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sour_spicy_noodles.3=Add-on requirement: the vinegar comes from Kaleidoscope Tavern. Without a matching vinegar item, this recipe is not registered.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sour_spicy_noodles.4=Eating effects: Warmth 45 seconds
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:special_seasoning=Seasoning Bottle & Special Seasoning
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:special_seasoning.1=First grind Green Chili Powder and Onion Powder (Food → Millstone); harvest Sichuan Pepper for direct use. See Workstations → Millstone & Grinding for the full setup. Place an Empty Seasoning Bottle and add ingredients to the top bottle. Each bottle stores up to 8 ingredients, and up to 4 bottles can be stacked in the world.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:special_seasoning.2=A finished seasoning requires at least one Green Chili Powder, one Sichuan Pepper, and one Onion Powder. Once all three bases are present, it becomes Seasoning to Be Shaken.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:special_seasoning.3=Take the pending bottle with an empty hand and hold use for 4 seconds. Sound and particles mark completion; the finished bottle has 16 uses. Releasing early does not finish it. Inventory bottle icons show the remaining amount. Check the held or placed layers for the actual ingredient order and colors.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:special_seasoning.4=Seasoning a grill costs 1 use per skewer currently on the grill; insufficient remaining uses do not partially commit.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:special_seasoning.5=Mixing: Redstone grants Speed, Gunpowder grants Strength, and Houttuynia Powder extends effects. Totem and Dragon Egg Powders add special effects; see their material entries for thresholds.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:special_seasoning.6=If you add the wrong ingredient or lack a base ingredient, pick up the bottle with an empty hand, place that bottle alone in a crafting grid, and take the empty-bottle output. Partially filled, pending, and used finished bottles can all be cleared. This discards every ingredient in the bottle; powders are not refunded, and individual ingredients cannot be removed.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:special_seasoning.7=Empty bottle: one wooden button centered above two full rows of glass. All eleven Java 1.21.1 wooden button variants are supported.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:special_seasoning.8=The server can disable hot-food and seasoning integration for Cookery dishes. New pot and stockpot outputs then receive no added heat or seasoning. Seasoning attempts show a disabled message without using the bottle. Grill seasoning is unchanged.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:squid_tentacle=Squid Tentacle
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:squid_tentacle.1=Acquisition: kill a normal squid while holding a Cookery Kitchen Knife in the main hand for a chance of tentacle drops; Looting affects the count.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:sugared_tomato=Sugared Tomato
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sugared_tomato.1=Shapeless crafting: 1 Cookery Tomato + 1 Sugar → 1 Sugared Tomato. Get tomato seeds from short grass while wearing a Cookery straw hat; plant on farmland and harvest when mature.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:sweet_potato=Sweet Potato
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sweet_potato.1=Acquisition and farming: break short grass in Survival while wearing a Cookery Straw Hat for a chance to obtain it. Plant on farmland and harvest when mature.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sweet_potato.2=Mill Sweet Potato in the Cookery Millstone to obtain Sweet Potato Powder.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sweet_potato.3=Sweet Potato can also be cooked in a furnace, smoker, campfire, or soul campfire into Roasted Sweet Potato, which grants about 30 seconds of Warmth.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:sweet_potato_powder=Sweet Potato Powder
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sweet_potato_powder.1=Required setup: install the complete family bundle for this release, containing Cookery 1.6.1 with the millstone compatibility repair already applied. Updating Grilling alone, or enabling the compatibility pack alongside untouched Cookery, does not fix input loading.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sweet_potato_powder.2=Grinding: hold Sweet Potato in your main hand and use it on a Cookery Millstone. Load up to 8 of the same input; each produces 1 Sweet Potato Powder. Use the raw input directly: no drying or roasting step, and no vanilla Grindstone.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sweet_potato_powder.3=Bring an adult cow or sheep onto the intact 3×3 millstone. Horses/donkeys must be tamed and unridden. A worker drives the loaded batch for about 100 ticks (5 seconds); collect powder ejected at the front. Sneak-use with an empty hand releases the worker. See Workstations → Millstone & Grinding for crafting and troubleshooting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:sweet_potato_powder.4=Cut Sweet Potato Powder 4 times on a Cookery Chopping Board to make Raw Sweet Potato Sheet, or hold-use the powder for about 1.5 seconds to knead it directly.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:totem_powder=Totem Powder
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:totem_powder.1=Required setup: install the complete family bundle for this release, containing Cookery 1.6.1 with the millstone compatibility repair already applied. Updating Grilling alone, or enabling the compatibility pack alongside untouched Cookery, does not fix input loading.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:totem_powder.2=Evokers drop Totems of Undying. Grinding consumes the totem itself and yields 1 powder.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:totem_powder.3=Grinding: hold Totem of Undying in your main hand and use it on a Cookery Millstone. Load up to 8 of the same input; each produces 1 Totem Powder. Use the raw input directly: no drying or roasting step, and no vanilla Grindstone.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:totem_powder.4=Bring an adult cow or sheep onto the intact 3×3 millstone. Horses/donkeys must be tamed and unridden. A worker drives the loaded batch for about 100 ticks (5 seconds); collect powder ejected at the front. Sneak-use with an empty hand releases the worker. See Workstations → Millstone & Grinding for crafting and troubleshooting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:totem_powder.5=Add Totem Powder to seasoning and eat it hot to gain the Heavy Metal survival effect.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:totem_powder.6=Damage confirmed as lethal consumes the survival effect once and sets health to 1.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:totem_powder.7=After triggering, Heavy Metal Poisoning lasts about 10 minutes; using more of the same survival seasoning does not bypass that poisoned state.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:totem_powder.8=Damage absorption and native Totem ordering are not fully matched. A partly spent absorption shield can still prevent this effect from triggering in time.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:unfinished_skewer=Unfinished Skewer
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:unfinished_skewer.1=On Bedrock, craft 1 stick into 1 empty Unfinished Skewer and place it in the offhand. Hold an ingredient in the main hand and use a block to thread it. Sneak-use can refund an empty skewer as a stick.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:unfinished_skewer.2=A skewer holds at most 3 ingredients. A matching fixed recipe resolves immediately; three ingredients that do not match a fixed recipe become a Secret Skewer.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:unfinished_skewer.3=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:wedding_candy=Wedding Candy
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:wedding_candy.1=Availability: the coded event runs September 1–12, 2026, Shanghai time. On day d, d minutes online awards d candies once that day. This is not a year-round crafting recipe.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:wedding_candy.2=Eating effects: Invincibility 15 seconds
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:grill=Grill
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:grill.1=Crafting pattern (· = empty): III / BCB / I·I; I = Iron Ingot, B = Brick, C = Coal or Charcoal. Shortest flow: light with Flint and Steel → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Cookery Oil Pot.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:grill.2=Use an empty hand to flip. There is about a 1-second flip cooldown; flip 4 times total.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:grill.3=After the fourth flip, use Special Seasoning. Oil points and seasoning uses are consumed per skewer on the grill.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:grill.4=After seasoning, use an empty hand to extract; sneak with an empty hand to extract repeatedly. Grill stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:grill.5=If a stage is not advanced for about 40 seconds, the skewers become overcooked; they can still be extracted as Dark Grilling.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:grill.6=Keep an overcooked batch heating for about 20 more seconds and it burns into charcoal.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:grill.7=If you need to stop, extinguish the grill with a shovel. Timers do not advance while it is unlit. Breaking mid-process: unoiled returns raw skewers; completed returns cooked; overcooked returns Dark Grilling; other oiled intermediate stages return Mysterious Skewers.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:grill.8=The server can select vanilla eating mode. With custom eating animations disabled, skewers use a 1.25-second native use action without the custom sounds or progress bar. Releasing a cancelled use adds no extra item debit.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_press=Wooden Oil Press
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_press.1=First make Oil Cake: surround 1 Wheat with 8 Canola Powder. The Oil Press must be loaded with all 4 cakes before pressing.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_press.2=A batch needs 16 progress: an anvil adds 4; Stone, Cobblestone, Deepslate, Cobbled Deepslate, or Blackstone adds 1 per press. After reaching 16, wait another 10 game ticks (about 0.5 seconds) for the oil.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_press.3=A completed batch produces 4 buckets of Canola Oil and 4 Oil Residue, but a nearby Big Vat must be able to accept all 4 buckets at once.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_press.4=If no vat is available, it is full, or it contains another fluid, the press waits. Fix the container and interact again to retry.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_press.5=Crafting-table pattern (· = empty):\nLIL\nF·G\nLHL\nL = Any log; I = Iron Ingot; F and G = Any supported fences, including mixed types; H = Hopper
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:oil_press.6=Supports 12 vanilla fence types: Oak, Spruce, Birch, Jungle, Acacia, Dark Oak, Mangrove, Cherry, Bamboo, Crimson, Warped, and Nether Brick. The two fence slots may use different types.
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:big_vat=Big Vat
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:big_vat.1=A Big Vat holds 8 buckets and only one fluid type at a time: water, lava, Canola Oil, Secret Chili Oil, or Premium Chili Oil.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:big_vat.2=Use the matching bucket to fill or extract it; use an empty hand to view its current bucket count and capacity.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:big_vat.3=The three Grilling oils can fill a Cookery Oil Pot directly: each vat bucket adds 8 oil points.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:big_vat.4=Breaking a filled vat preserves its fluid type and amount on the dropped vat item; placing it again restores the contents.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:big_vat.5=Craft with 7 Brick items and 1 Bucket. Crafting-table pattern (· = empty):\nB·B\nBUB\nBBB\nB = Brick; U = Bucket
guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_sapling=Sichuan Pepper Tree
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_sapling.1=Find your first pepper tree in newly generated biomes tagged as forest. Generation is random and does not retrofit explored terrain. Harvest fruiting leaves for pepper; breaking leaves can drop saplings for replanting.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_sapling.2=Plant a Sichuan Pepper Sapling on a dirt-like block. At light level 9 or higher it can grow randomly. Bone Meal can attempt to advance growth; Oil Residue makes two consecutive attempts.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_sapling.3=Use an empty hand on fruiting leaves to harvest 1–2 Sichuan Pepper, returning the leaves to an unfruited state.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_sapling.4=Pepper leaves sting: stepping on them briefly slows and damages entities, except foxes and bees.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_sapling.5=Acquisition: pepper leaves can drop saplings; shears or Silk Touch recover the leaf block. A pepper log crafts into 4 oak planks.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_sapling.6=Naturally grown leaves decay when no nearby pepper log supports them. Decay has a 10% chance to drop a sapling and a 2% chance to drop a stick; fruiting leaves also drop 1 Sichuan Pepper. Player-placed leaves do not decay.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_grilling:pepper_sapling.7=Pepper saplings and leaves can both go into a Composter. Each item has a 30% chance to raise the compost level by one.
guide.kg.name.minecraft:redstone=Redstone Dust
guide.kg.body.minecraft:redstone.1=With 1–3 Redstone in the seasoning, eating it hot grants Speed I for a base duration of about 3 minutes.
guide.kg.body.minecraft:redstone.2=At 4 or more Redstone, it becomes Speed II.
guide.kg.body.minecraft:redstone.3=Houttuynia Powder can further extend this seasoning-effect duration.
guide.kg.name.minecraft:gunpowder=Gunpowder
guide.kg.body.minecraft:gunpowder.1=With 1–3 Gunpowder in the seasoning, eating it hot grants Strength I for a base duration of about 3 minutes.
guide.kg.body.minecraft:gunpowder.2=At 4 or more Gunpowder, it becomes Strength II.
guide.kg.body.minecraft:gunpowder.3=Houttuynia Powder can further extend this seasoning-effect duration.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_quick_start=Six-step grill flow
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_quick_start.1=Start with a Fish Skewer: obtain one raw Cod or Salmon. Beef Chunks and Chicken Skin can also be obtained on the Cookery Chopping Board as described in their entries.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_quick_start.2=Prepare a Grill, Flint and Steel, a filled Oil Pot and finished Special Seasoning first. See the Oil Pot and Seasoning Bottle entries for their prerequisites.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_quick_start.3=Craft one stick into an empty Unfinished Skewer and equip it offhand. Hold the raw fish in the main hand and use it on a block. On Windows use the use key; on touch controls interact with the block.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_quick_start.4=Light the grill → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Oil Pot. Oil costs one point per skewer.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_quick_start.5=Use an empty hand to flip four times, with about one second between flips. After the fourth flip, apply Special Seasoning: one use per skewer.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_quick_start.6=Take finished skewers with an empty hand; sneak to take them repeatedly. Eat while warm; remaining heat appears in the item lore. Unattended food burns and stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_quick_start.7=Hold use to eat: release before 1.25 seconds to cancel, or after that checkpoint to consume. The full animation takes about 4.5–5 seconds. Release sneak for normal eating.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_quick_start.8=For automatic threading, craft four paper in a 2×2 square into a blank Skewer Recipe Book, then follow its recording and crafting page.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_hot_food=Hot Food & the three oils
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_hot_food.1=Canola Oil gives about 60 seconds of Hot Food time, Secret Chili Oil about 10 minutes, and Premium Chili Oil about 20 minutes. Remaining heat is shown on the food lore. New heating and hot-food merges round the expiry down to five-second boundaries, as in Java. Previously saved deadlines remain exact on reads; reheating, merging or refrigerator sorting re-buckets them as in Java.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_hot_food.2=When eaten hot, newly gained fixed skewer effects have double duration and newly gained saturation is increased by 25%.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_hot_food.3=Special Seasoning effects only trigger while the food is still hot; Hot Food does not double those seasoning durations a second time. Cold food remains edible, but those seasoning effects do not activate.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_hot_food.4=A Secret Chili Oil Bucket is shapelessly crafted from 1 Canola Oil Bucket + 3 Red Chili Powder. All three oils can use the supported bucket, Big Vat, and Cookery Oil Pot transfer paths.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_hot_food.5=Hot skewers do not freely merge with cold skewers or stacks whose remaining heat is very different.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_hot_food.6=Sneak-use a Chest, Trapped Chest, or Barrel with an empty hand to sort skewers. Hot stacks only merge when their remaining Hot Food time differs by at most 5 minutes.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_hot_food.7=Merged heat is a count-weighted average, so one fresh skewer cannot instantly refresh a whole old stack.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_hot_food.8=With an empty offhand, sneak-use hot food to merge inventory stacks with matching item data using count-weighted heat. This includes foods other than skewers and is not limited by the chest sorting five-minute window. Release sneak to eat.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_recipe_beef=Beef Skewer
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_beef.1=With Cookery 1.6.1 and the family Chopping Board extension, place one raw Beef on the board, cut four times with a Kitchen Knife, then use the knife once more to release two Beef Chunks. The chunks replace this input's normal Cow Offal output.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_beef.2=Nutrition panel: cooked skewer. Raw: hunger 2, saturation 1.2; cooked: hunger 5, saturation 6.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_beef.3=Ingredient order: Beef Chunks → Red Chili → Beef Chunks
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_beef.4=Craft an empty Unfinished Skewer from one stick and equip it offhand. Hold a skewerable ingredient in the main hand and use it on a block to add one ingredient. Shortest flow: light with Flint and Steel → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Cookery Oil Pot.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_beef.5=Use an empty hand to flip. There is about a 1-second flip cooldown; flip 4 times total. After the fourth flip, use Special Seasoning. Oil points and seasoning uses are consumed per skewer on the grill. After seasoning, use an empty hand to extract; sneak with an empty hand to extract repeatedly. Grill stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_beef.6=Cooked effect: Strength · base 10 seconds.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_beef.7=When eaten hot, newly gained fixed skewer effects have double duration and newly gained saturation is increased by 25%. Special Seasoning effects only trigger while the food is still hot; Hot Food does not double those seasoning durations a second time. Cold food remains edible, but those seasoning effects do not activate.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_beef.8=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_recipe_pork_belly=Pork Belly Skewer
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_pork_belly.1=Nutrition panel: cooked skewer. Raw: hunger 2, saturation 1.2; cooked: hunger 5, saturation 6.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_pork_belly.2=Ingredient order: Raw Pork Belly → Green Chili → Raw Pork Belly
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_pork_belly.3=Craft an empty Unfinished Skewer from one stick and equip it offhand. Hold a skewerable ingredient in the main hand and use it on a block to add one ingredient. Shortest flow: light with Flint and Steel → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Cookery Oil Pot.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_pork_belly.4=Use an empty hand to flip. There is about a 1-second flip cooldown; flip 4 times total. After the fourth flip, use Special Seasoning. Oil points and seasoning uses are consumed per skewer on the grill. After seasoning, use an empty hand to extract; sneak with an empty hand to extract repeatedly. Grill stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_pork_belly.5=Cooked effect: Vigor · base 30 seconds; suppresses hunger/saturation loss while sprinting.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_pork_belly.6=When eaten hot, newly gained fixed skewer effects have double duration and newly gained saturation is increased by 25%. Special Seasoning effects only trigger while the food is still hot; Hot Food does not double those seasoning durations a second time. Cold food remains edible, but those seasoning effects do not activate.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_pork_belly.7=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_recipe_chicken_skin=Chicken Skin Skewer
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_chicken_skin.1=With Cookery 1.6.1 and the family Chopping Board extension, place one raw Chicken on the board, cut four times with a Kitchen Knife, then use the knife once more to release the original three Raw Meat Cuts and one Bone, plus 1–3 Chicken Skin. Killing chickens does not yield skin.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_chicken_skin.2=Nutrition panel: cooked skewer. Raw: hunger 2, saturation 1; cooked: hunger 4, saturation 4.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_chicken_skin.3=Ingredient order: Chicken Skin → Chicken Skin
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_chicken_skin.4=Craft an empty Unfinished Skewer from one stick and equip it offhand. Hold a skewerable ingredient in the main hand and use it on a block to add one ingredient. Shortest flow: light with Flint and Steel → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Cookery Oil Pot.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_chicken_skin.5=Use an empty hand to flip. There is about a 1-second flip cooldown; flip 4 times total. After the fourth flip, use Special Seasoning. Oil points and seasoning uses are consumed per skewer on the grill. After seasoning, use an empty hand to extract; sneak with an empty hand to extract repeatedly. Grill stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_chicken_skin.6=Cooked effect: Speed · base 20 seconds.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_chicken_skin.7=When eaten hot, newly gained fixed skewer effects have double duration and newly gained saturation is increased by 25%. Special Seasoning effects only trigger while the food is still hot; Hot Food does not double those seasoning durations a second time. Cold food remains edible, but those seasoning effects do not activate.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_chicken_skin.8=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_recipe_mid_wing=Mid-Wing Skewer
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_mid_wing.1=Nutrition panel: cooked skewer. Raw: hunger 3, saturation 0.6426; cooked: hunger 7, saturation 3.0002.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_mid_wing.2=Ingredient order: Chicken Wing → Red Chili → Chicken Wing
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_mid_wing.3=Craft an empty Unfinished Skewer from one stick and equip it offhand. Hold a skewerable ingredient in the main hand and use it on a block to add one ingredient. Shortest flow: light with Flint and Steel → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Cookery Oil Pot.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_mid_wing.4=Use an empty hand to flip. There is about a 1-second flip cooldown; flip 4 times total. After the fourth flip, use Special Seasoning. Oil points and seasoning uses are consumed per skewer on the grill. After seasoning, use an empty hand to extract; sneak with an empty hand to extract repeatedly. Grill stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_mid_wing.5=Cooked effect: Mustard · base 45 seconds; creepers within about 6 blocks are pushed away.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_mid_wing.6=When eaten hot, newly gained fixed skewer effects have double duration and newly gained saturation is increased by 25%. Special Seasoning effects only trigger while the food is still hot; Hot Food does not double those seasoning durations a second time. Cold food remains edible, but those seasoning effects do not activate.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_mid_wing.7=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_recipe_squid_tentacle=Squid Tentacle Skewer
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_squid_tentacle.1=Nutrition panel: cooked skewer. Raw: hunger 2, saturation 0.8; cooked: hunger 5, saturation 4.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_squid_tentacle.2=Ingredient order: Squid Tentacle → Squid Tentacle → Squid Tentacle
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_squid_tentacle.3=Craft an empty Unfinished Skewer from one stick and equip it offhand. Hold a skewerable ingredient in the main hand and use it on a block to add one ingredient. Shortest flow: light with Flint and Steel → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Cookery Oil Pot.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_squid_tentacle.4=Use an empty hand to flip. There is about a 1-second flip cooldown; flip 4 times total. After the fourth flip, use Special Seasoning. Oil points and seasoning uses are consumed per skewer on the grill. After seasoning, use an empty hand to extract; sneak with an empty hand to extract repeatedly. Grill stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_squid_tentacle.5=Cooked effect: Water Breathing · base 30 seconds.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_squid_tentacle.6=When eaten hot, newly gained fixed skewer effects have double duration and newly gained saturation is increased by 25%. Special Seasoning effects only trigger while the food is still hot; Hot Food does not double those seasoning durations a second time. Cold food remains edible, but those seasoning effects do not activate.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_squid_tentacle.7=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_recipe_fish=Fish Skewer
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_fish.1=Nutrition panel: cooked skewer. Raw: hunger 3, saturation 1.35; cooked: hunger 6, saturation 5.4.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_fish.2=Ingredient order: Cod / Salmon / Tropical Fish / Pufferfish (choose 1)
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_fish.3=Craft an empty Unfinished Skewer from one stick and equip it offhand. Hold a skewerable ingredient in the main hand and use it on a block to add one ingredient. Shortest flow: light with Flint and Steel → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Cookery Oil Pot.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_fish.4=Use an empty hand to flip. There is about a 1-second flip cooldown; flip 4 times total. After the fourth flip, use Special Seasoning. Oil points and seasoning uses are consumed per skewer on the grill. After seasoning, use an empty hand to extract; sneak with an empty hand to extract repeatedly. Grill stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_fish.5=Cooked effect: Tundra Strider · base 30 seconds; faster on snow/ice and helps with Powder Snow.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_fish.6=When eaten hot, newly gained fixed skewer effects have double duration and newly gained saturation is increased by 25%. Special Seasoning effects only trigger while the food is still hot; Hot Food does not double those seasoning durations a second time. Cold food remains edible, but those seasoning effects do not activate.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_fish.7=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet=Sweet Potato Sheet Skewer
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet.1=Nutrition panel: cooked skewer. Raw: hunger 3, saturation 3.4998; cooked: hunger 6, saturation 14.0004.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet.2=Ingredient order: Raw Sweet Potato Sheet → Minced Houttuynia → Minced Houttuynia
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet.3=Craft an empty Unfinished Skewer from one stick and equip it offhand. Hold a skewerable ingredient in the main hand and use it on a block to add one ingredient. Shortest flow: light with Flint and Steel → insert 1–3 raw skewers → brush with a filled Cookery Oil Pot.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet.4=Use an empty hand to flip. There is about a 1-second flip cooldown; flip 4 times total. After the fourth flip, use Special Seasoning. Oil points and seasoning uses are consumed per skewer on the grill. After seasoning, use an empty hand to extract; sneak with an empty hand to extract repeatedly. Grill stages cannot be skipped.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet.5=Cooked effect: Preservation · base 45 seconds; removes hunger/poison/nausea-style penalties from dangerous foods.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet.6=When eaten hot, newly gained fixed skewer effects have double duration and newly gained saturation is increased by 25%. Special Seasoning effects only trigger while the food is still hot; Hot Food does not double those seasoning durations a second time. Cold food remains edible, but those seasoning effects do not activate.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_recipe_sweet_potato_sheet.7=Uncooked unfinished, fixed-raw, and Secret skewers can be sneak-disassembled to recover their ingredients and stick.
