guide.kg.name.kaleidoscope_cookery:oil_pot_filled=Cookery Oil Pot: Grilling Oils
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_cookery:oil_pot_filled.1=Use the host guide for the Oil Pot recipe. The family API shares one oil payload between Cookery and Grilling.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_cookery:oil_pot_filled.2=Fat capacity is 256 points; Grilling fluid capacity is 64. Hold an oil bucket in the main hand and an empty pot offhand, then use: each bucket adds 8 points. An empty pot can also draw from a source or Big Vat.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_cookery:oil_pot_filled.3=Placed pots accept matching oil buckets at 8 points each. Fat and the three Grilling oils cannot mix. Empty-hand clicks on a typed placed pot do not dispense fat.
guide.kg.body.kaleidoscope_cookery:oil_pot_filled.4=Brush the grill with a filled pot: one point per loaded skewer. Fat and Canola retain heat for 1 minute, Chili for 10, Premium Chili for 20. Exhaustion returns an empty pot; breaking a placed pot preserves oil type and quantity.
guide.kg.name.kg_a1:guide_millstone=Millstone & Grinding
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_millstone.1=Required setup: install the complete family bundle for this release, containing Cookery 1.6.1 with the millstone compatibility repair already applied. Updating Grilling alone, or enabling the compatibility pack alongside untouched Cookery, does not fix input loading.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_millstone.2=Craft a Cookery Millstone on a crafting table (· = empty):\n·F·\nSG·\nTTT\nF = wooden fence, S = stick, G = vanilla Grindstone, T = smooth stone. Reserve a clear 3×3 footprint.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_millstone.3=Hold input → use the millstone (up to 8 identical items) → bring an adult cow/sheep onto it → wait about 100 ticks → collect powder at the front. Horses/donkeys must be tamed and unridden; baby animals cannot drive it.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_millstone.4=Recipes: canola seeds→canola powder; onion→onion powder; red/green chili→matching chili powder; houttuynia→houttuynia powder; sweet potato→sweet potato powder; totem→totem powder. Each input yields 1 powder, without drying or roasting.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_millstone.5=Sichuan Pepper goes directly into the bottle. Dragon Egg Powder uses a kitchen knife on a dragon egg. Vanilla redstone and gunpowder also go in directly. A finished seasoning needs Green Chili Powder, Sichuan Pepper and Onion Powder.
guide.kg.body.kg_a1:guide_millstone.6=Not turning? Check the intact footprint, adult worker, riders and another millstone binding. If no worker is found within 30 seconds, the input is returned. Sneak-use empty-handed releases a worker. Inputs rejected? The family compatibility pack must include the extension-input fix; unpatched Cookery 1.6.1 registers recipes but rejects these inputs.
## END GRILLING GUIDE A3 (generated)
